        "original_id": "2980781c-6ebb-5d05-a1dc-4993df88d2fc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ivan Rival, Dwight Duffus\n- Organizations: University of Calgary, University of Ottawa, Emory University\n- Places: Ottawa, Ontario, Canada, Sandy Hill, Rideau Canal\n- Products: Order (journal)\n- Roles: professor of mathematics, professor of computer science, editor in chief\n\nFacts:\n- Ivan Rival was born on March 15, 1947, and he died on January 22, 2002 in Ottawa, Ontario, Canada.\n- Ivan Rival was a Canadian mathematician and computer scientist.\n- Ivan Rival was a professor of mathematics at the University of Calgary and a professor of computer science at the University of Ottawa.\n- Order was founded in 1984 by University of Calgary mathematics professor Ivan Rival.\n- As of 2010, Dwight Duffus was the editor in chief of Order.\n- Dwight Duffus was the Goodrich C. White Professor of Mathematics and Computer Science at Emory University and a former student of Ivan Rival.\n- The main campus of the University of Ottawa is located on 42.5 hectares in the residential neighbourhood of Sandy Hill, adjacent to Ottawa's Rideau Canal.",
